@flexiarg snatch/probe-before-committing
@title Probe Before Committing
@audience players, policy authors
@tone practical
@style pattern
@why snatch/protect-the-unprotected-move

! conclusion: Make the first offer the smallest one that still discriminates, and read it as information rather than as trade.

  + context: **Play grain** — the antecedent is a game state, not a design
    question. Snatch or Share, any treatment, first encounter with a counterpart
    whose disposition is unknown.

  + IF:
    You face a counterpart whose disposition you do not know, and an offer of any
    size is available to you.

  + HOWEVER:
    A large first offer is unrecoverable if they snatch, and a zero offer buys
    nothing — you end the round knowing exactly what you knew at its start.

  + THEN:
    Offer the smallest amount whose acceptance and whose seizure would look
    different to you, and treat the response as the thing you bought.

  + BECAUSE:
    The first exchange with an unknown counterpart is priced as information, not
    as trade. One token buys a clean read; ten tokens buy the same read and cost
    nine more.
    + evidence: item `S-001` (`futon3/checks/item-s001.edn`) states this policy's
      predicted distribution in advance and collapses a two-point spread to zero
      on either accept or snatch.
